    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "\n## 🧠 Overview\n\nThis workflow is an AI-powered personal productivity assistant that converts voice or text inputs from Telegram into structured actions such as **email generation** and **calendar event scheduling**, using local LLMs (Ollama), speech-to-text (Whisper), and human-in-the-loop approval.\n\nIt acts as a unified assistant for communication and scheduling, enabling users to manage emails and calendar events directly through natural language voice commands.\n\n---\n\n## ⚙️ Workflow Capabilities\n\nThe system supports two core automation modes:\n\n### 📧 Email Automation\n- Converts voice into structured professional emails\n- Extracts recipient, subject, and body\n  \n- Sends for human approval before dispatch\n- Sends final email via Gmail\n\n---\n\n### 📅 Calendar Automation\n- Converts user instructions into structured calendar events\n- Extracts title, date, time, duration, location, and description\n- Sends event details for approval via Telegram\n- Creates event after confirmation\n\n---\n\n## 🏗️ Workflow Architecture\n\n---\n\n## 🎤 1. Voice Input Capture (Telegram Trigger)\n\nUsers send voice messages or text instructions via Telegram.\n\n- Accepts natural language input\n- Supports both email and calendar requests\n- Acts as the entry point for the workflow\n\n---\n\n## 🎧 2. Speech-to-Text Processing (Whisper API)\n\nVoice messages are processed using Whisper ASR.\n\n- Converts audio → text\n- Ensures accurate transcription\n- Passes clean text to AI classification layer\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 3. Intent Classification Layer (AI Router)\n\nThe system classifies user intent into:\n\n- 📧 Email Request\n- 📅 Calendar Event Request\n- 💬 General Conversation\n\nThis enables dynamic routing of tasks.\n\n---\n\n## ✉️ 4. Email Generation Pipeline (AI Agent)\n\nIf intent = Email:\n\n- Extracts structured email fields:\n  - recipient\n  - subject\n  - body\n- Ensures professional tone and formatting\n- Outputs structured JSON\n\n",
        "height": 1712,
        "width": 624,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "65b5996c-d92e-4eb0-b9bd-f60a7cb8fef3",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
